As stated a few weeks ago, I have other reasons as well for continuing
to use Outlook Express. The most important reason is that I archive
almost all my e-mail and selected newsmessages. I like to have my e-mail
and news in the same program, so I can file them in the same folder
structures. This way, I can keep my reactions (posts and e-mails) and
the original posts together in the same folders.

Most other programs I have looked at for e-mail *and* news don't offer
that possibility, and if they do, they have no easy way to convert my
archive without losing the directory structure. With an archive that
goes back over more than ten years, re-sorting by hand would cost me
more than a month of my spare time, which I am *not* willing to invest
just because other people are trying to pressure me into using another
newsreader.

Finally, if my boss would catch me using a USB drive, I could be in
trouble. They have reasons for not allowing us to use non-approved
software, and the fact that I didn't install it on my laptop but instead
ran if off a pen drive wouldn't change those reasons.

